======================================================================
 Third-party components
======================================================================

The authoritative, machine-readable inventory of every dependency —
name, version, license expression, SHA-256 checksum, dependency graph
and target coverage — is maintained at:

    docs/sbom/sbom.cdx.json             CycloneDX 1.5 SBOM
    docs/sbom/dependency-inventory.tsv  flat audit table
    docs/sbom/LICENSE-REPORT.md         analysis and obligations

Source distributions pull dependencies from crates.io, where each
package's license text ships inside its .crate archive. Binary
distributions must additionally carry the texts called out below;
vendored copies live in third-party/ at the repository root.

--- EPL-2.0 -----------------------------------------------------------

merman-elk-layered 0.8.0-alpha.7 (reached via merman's `layout-elk`
feature, enabled by docgen-mermaid) is licensed under the Eclipse
Public License 2.0 — text at third-party/EPL-2.0.txt. It is used as an
unmodified crates.io dependency; EPL-2.0 terms apply to that component
and modifications of it, not to docgen itself.

--- MPL-2.0 -----------------------------------------------------------

cssparser, cssparser-macros, dtoa-short and selectors (reached via
lol_html in merman-core) are Mozilla Public License 2.0 — text at
third-party/MPL-2.0.txt. MPL is file-level copyleft: covered files
stay MPL-2.0 when redistributed.

--- Fonts embedded from typst-assets 0.15.1 (feature "fonts") ---------

The binaries bundle typefaces under several free font licenses, and
generated PDFs subset-embed them: Libertinus Serif (SIL OFL 1.1),
NewComputerModern and DejaVu (GUST Font License 1.0), NewCM10-Regular
(GPL-3.0-or-later with GUST Font Exception and Distribution
Exception), the PDF base-14 Foxit fonts (BSD-3-Clause, PDFium/Google)
and ICC profiles / data tables (CC0-1.0). The complete upstream NOTICE
with all license texts is vendored verbatim at
third-party/NOTICE.typst-assets and must be redistributed with any
binary that embeds these fonts.

--- Fonts bundled in docgen-excalidraw --------------------------------

crates/docgen-excalidraw/assets/*.ttf (Excalifont, Virgil, Nunito,
Cascadia, Liberation Sans — subset conversions of the
@excalidraw/excalidraw npm fonts) are MIT / SIL OFL 1.1; texts and
per-font copyright and Reserved-Font-Name notices live in
crates/docgen-excalidraw/assets/LICENSES/.

--- Everything else ---------------------------------------------------

All remaining dependencies are MIT, Apache-2.0 (including
"Apache-2.0 WITH LLVM-exception", e.g. the wasmtime/cranelift stack),
BSD-2/3-Clause, ISC, Zlib, Unicode-3.0, CC0-1.0, BSL-1.0, Unlicense,
or dual combinations whose permissive branch applies; the SBOM records
the exact per-package expression. ittapi/ittapi-sys (GPL-2.0-only OR
BSD-3-Clause; BSD branch) are dev-only test tooling and are never
distributed.
